<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="60d7d3ab">Once agreed in the planning phases, the criteria should be monitored and updated through the organization or program
governance structure. As go-live nears, the criteria will be monitored daily.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="4b92866"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="119599c7"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="51e7e2c5">&lt;p&gt;
    The cutover readiness criteria are metrics against which the organization&apos;s readiness to proceed with the transition,
    or phase will be measured. The criteria provide a measure of how ready the organization is to accept a new solution and
    how ready the program is to deploy it.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The criteria should be categorized into broad headings such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Processes are proven
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Systems are ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Business is ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        People are ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Data is ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Technology infrastructure is proven
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
